# hcrulepy coverage supplement - functions NOT exercised by all.rules
# Input word for capture: p@ssW0rd   (length 8; chars p @ s s W 0 r d)
#
# IMPORTANT (discovered 2026-08-12 against real hashcat v7.1.2): running
# this file STANDALONE makes hashcat abort with "No valid rules left" and
# produce ZERO output/warnings, even though several of these rules ARE
# individually supported by hashcat's --stdout -r engine. hashcat's rule
# engine behaves differently for small rule files than for large ones - the
# same rules (M4, l<9$5, etc.) DO work when appended to a large existing
# ruleset (e.g. all.rules) instead of run alone. See
# tests/test_hashcat_verified_functions.py for the confirmed results.
#
# To capture meaningfully, APPEND this file's content to all.rules first:
#   printf 'p@ssW0rd\n' > word.txt
#   cat all.rules coverage_supplement.rule > combined.rule
#   hashcat --stdout -r combined.rule word.txt > coverage_supplement.out
# (then diff the tail against all.rules-only output to isolate these rules'
# contributions - see tests/test_hashcat_verified_functions.py's docstring
# for the exact probe-marker technique used to do this unambiguously.)
#
# Also confirmed NOT processed by hashcat's -r engine at all (no output, no
# warning, even when appended to a large ruleset): X, (, ), =, %. hcrulepy
# still implements them per the wiki; they just cannot be verified against
# real hashcat by this method.
#
# Rejection rules that REJECT produce NO output line (that is the point).
# Rules that pass emit the transformed candidate. Keep comments/blank lines -
# hashcat ignores them, and so does hcrulepy.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------- memory: M 4 6
# M = memorize; 4 = append memory; 6 = prepend memory
M4
lM4
uMl4
rMr6
uMl6
lM6
# X = insert substring of memory (may be skipped by hashcat's OpenCL rule
# engine, exactly like lMuX084 in all.rules; kept so the capture shows whether
# this build supports it).
lMX084
# ------------------------------------------------------------------ memory: Q
# Q = reject if the memorized word equals the current word.
# MQ: memory == word  -> REJECT (no output)
MQ
# MlQ: memorize "p@ssW0rd", lowercase -> "p@ssw0rd" != memory -> PASS
MlQ
# uMlQ: memorize "P@SSW0RD", lowercase -> "p@ssw0rd" != memory -> PASS
uMlQ
# ----------------------------------------------------------- reject length: < > _
# <N reject if len > N   (len is 8)
<9
<8
<7
# >N reject if len < N
>7
>8
>9
# _N reject if len != N
_8
_7
# --------------------------------------------------------- reject contains: ! /
# !X reject if X present
!z
!s
# /X reject if X absent
/s
/z
# ------------------------------------------------------ reject ends/starts: ( )
# (X reject unless starts with X
(p
(x
# )X reject unless ends with X
)d
)x
# ------------------------------------------------------ reject at position: = %
# =NX reject unless char at position N equals X
=0p
=1@
=7d
=0x
# %NX reject if X occurs fewer than N times
%1s
%2s
%3s
%1@
%2@
